{
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nobrega8/mbmap-library/main/schema/mbmap-2.schema.json",
  "mbmap": 2,
  "vendor": "Eurotherm",
  "model": "6000 series graphic recorders",
  "models": [
    "6100A",
    "6180A",
    "6100E"
  ],
  "vendor_website": "eurotherm.com",
  "description": "Paperless graphic recorder (100 mm / 180 mm): instrument data and run-time values of the input channels over Modbus TCP",
  "revision": 2,
  "revised": "2026-11-14",
  "source": "Eurotherm, 6100A/6180A Paperless graphic recorder User Guide, HA028910 issue 8 (October 2010), section 8",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "6100A/6180A Paperless graphic recorder User Guide",
      "version": "HA028910/8",
      "date": "2010-10",
      "url": "https://www.surecontrols.com/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/6100A-6180A_HA028910_8.pdf",
      "note": "section 8 (instrument data, channel run-time data); linked in issue #396"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "The issue names the vendor Ecil; the linked guide is the Eurotherm 6100A/6180A user guide (versions 5.1 and later), so the map is filed under Eurotherm.",
    "Modbus TCP slave (function codes 3 and 4, identical here, 6, 8 and 16). Addresses are given in the guide in hex and decimal and are used as written (address_base 0). Modbus security must be disabled (Operator/Config/Instrument) for communication to start, or a login register write is needed.",
    "Only the instrument data and the first 12 input channels are mapped: for each channel the value, status and alarm bits, the span limits and the decimal places. Run-time data of channel N is at A1D9 + 3 x (N-1) (value, status, alarm information); configuration of channel N is at the channel 1 address + 162 x (N-1). The guide covers input channels 1 to 75, maths, totalisers, counters, groups and a 32-bit IEEE area, which are not mapped.",
    "A value is a scaled 16-bit integer (plus or minus 32767); its decimal point comes from the channel's decimal places, and a value that does not fit is sent as 32767. The date and time (Double, 4 registers each) are not mapped.",
    "Written from the manufacturer's document; not tested on a device."
  ],
  "protocol": "tcp",
  "unit_id": 1,
  "port": 502,
  "address_base": 0,
  "byte_order": "big",
  "word_order": "big",
  "x_status": "official",
  "enums": {
    "chan_status": {"0": "Good PV", "1": "Channel off", "2": "Over range", "3": "Under range", "4": "Hardware error", "5": "Ranging error", "6": "Overflow", "7": "Bad PV", "8": "No data"}
  },
